": "pic.x.com/7TrXbEqhCK", "end": 289, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/WHO/status/2116455224101527659/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116455222427926528", "start": 266, "url": "https://t.co/7TrXbEqhCK"}]}, "id": "2116455224101527659", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 19, "impression_count": 44564, "like_count": 252, "quote_count": 8, "reply_count": 34, "retweet_count": 79}, "text": "Noncommunicable diseases (NCDs), like heart disease, diabetes, chronic respiratory diseases and cancers are some of the world’s silent killers 👻.\n\nThis Halloween, stay one step ahead—don’t let tobacco, alcohol, air pollution, or physical inactivity sneak up on you. https://t.co/7TrXbEqhCK", "url": "https://x.com/WHO/status/2116455224101527659"}, {"author_id": "207256884", "created_at": "2026-10-31T08:14:54.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116443783848181939"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/tDYHgMv4sQ", "end": 300, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/preskill/status/2116443783848181939/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116443450698842112", "start": 277, "url": "https://t.co/tDYHgMv4sQ"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/tDYHgMv4sQ", "end": 300, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/preskill/status/2116443783848181939/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116443499407220736", "start": 277, "url": "https://t.co/tDYHgMv4sQ"}]}, "id": "2116443783848181939", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 27, "impression_count": 14344, "like_count": 186, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 7, "retweet_count": 13}, "text": "We were in Aspen in June 2000 for a quantum computing program that David DiVincenzo and I organized. Daniel Gottesman and I were writing our paper about GKP codes, and Knill-Laflamme-Milburn were working on photonic quantum computing. You may recognize some of the luminaries. https://t.co/tDYHgMv4sQ", "url": "https://x.com/preskill/status/2116443783848181939"}, {"author_id": "32372834", "created_at": "2026-10-31T03:00:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116364545279000589"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 194, "id": "137777298", "start": 184, "username": "scisignal"}], "urls": [{"description": "Synaptic plasticity in Aplysia is accompanied by dynamic modification of neuronal tRNAs.", "display_url": "scim.ag/3UiULAO", "end": 218, "expanded_url": "https://scim.ag/3UiULAO", "images": [{"height": 550, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115458695983136769/1wC_VVB_?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 715}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115458695983136769/1wC_VVB_?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 195, "status": 200, "title": "Neuronal tRNA modifications in Aplysia californica are repatterned during behavioral habituation", "unwound_url": "https://www.science.org/doi/10.1126/scisignal.aed9028?utm_campaign=ScienceMagazine&utm_medium=ownedSocial&utm_source=twitter", "url": "https://t.co/v4h85QGzuN"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/D7FNvAWN3B", "end": 242, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/ScienceMagazine/status/2116364545279000589/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116364543546867712", "start": 219, "url": "https://t.co/D7FNvAWN3B"}]}, "id": "2116364545279000589", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 28, "impression_count": 23355, "like_count": 118, "quote_count": 4, "reply_count": 8, "retweet_count": 19}, "text": "By studying sea slugs in the lab, researchers have determined how structural changes in molecules called transfer RNAs accompany behavioral habituation, an elemental form of learning. @SciSignal https://t.co/v4h85QGzuN https://t.co/D7FNvAWN3B", "url": "https://x.com/ScienceMagazine/status/2116364545279000589"}, {"author_id": "32372834", "created_at": "2026-10-31T02:00:08.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116349472225538242"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 190, "start": 177, "tag": "ScienceBooks"}], "urls": [{"description": "Science shows us what to do to save the planet—poetry helps us understand why we should", "display_url": "scim.ag/4yMAwtk", "end": 235, "expanded_url": "https://scim.ag/4yMAwtk", "images": [{"height":